。每个边框内部除了黑色背景外，还散落着若干像素碎片，这些碎片的颜色与该边框不同，但与网格中另一个边框的颜色相同。每种碎片颜色在所有边框内部只出现一次（即每个边框内只有一种非背景碎片颜色）。\\\\\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个封闭矩形边框，找到其内部散落碎片的颜色 C_inner。将该边框的所有边框像素重新着色为 C_inner。同时，将边框内部的碎片像素替换为该边框原来的颜色 C_border。边框内部的背景像素保持黑色不变。\\\\\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现边框内碎片颜色与其他边框颜色之间的\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"颜色交换\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"映射关系，然后理解变换是边框与内部碎片之间的颜色互换——碎片的颜色告诉你边框该变成什么色，而边框的原色则回填到碎片位置上。\\\\\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n- `description`：每个带箭头标记的色块沿箭头方向\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"印章式\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"复制自身，复制次数由该色块内部孔洞的数量决定。\\\\\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不接触的单色连通色块（4-连通），每个色块是不规则形状，其中可能包含零个或多个由背景色形成的内部孔洞（被色块像素完全包围的黑色区域）。每个色块的外侧恰好有一个由 red 像素组成的箭头标记，箭头由三个像素构成：一个尖端像素和两个沿对角线分布的翼像素，整体指向上、下、左、右四个方向之一。箭头尖端与色块边缘恰好相邻（4-邻接）。\\\\\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个色块，数出其内部孔洞的数量 N。沿箭头指向的方向，在色块的前方，以色块自身的外接矩形宽度（或高度，取决于方向）加 1 格间距为步长，连续复制 N 份该色块的完整形状（包括孔洞保持为黑色）。若 N=0，则色块保持原样不复制。箭头标记在输出中被擦除（变为背景色）。色块本身保留在原位。\\\\\\\\n- `Key insight`：箭头仅提供复制方向，而复制次数这一关键信息隐藏在色块自身的拓扑结构中——内部孔洞数即为复制份数。解题者需要同时识别方向线索（箭头）和数量线索（孔洞），并理解它们分别控制变换的不同维度。\\\\\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n- `description`：将网格中由分隔线划分的若干面板按照隐含的拼图逻辑重新排列，使得相邻面板的边缘花纹能够无缝对接。\\\\\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格被 grey 色的单像素宽分隔线均匀划分为 m*n 个等大矩形面板（例如 2*3 或 3*3）。每个面板内部包含彩色图案，且每个面板的四条边缘（紧邻分隔线或网格边界的那一行/列像素）上有特定的颜色序列花纹。整个网格中恰好存在唯一一种排列方式，使得每对相邻面板的共享边缘花纹完全一致（即左面板的右边缘与右面板的左边缘像素逐一相同，上面板的下边缘与下面板的上边缘像素逐一相同）。输入中面板的排列是打乱的。\\\\\\\\n- `Rule`：找到所有面板的唯一正确排列，使得每对 4-邻接的面板共享边缘花纹完全匹配。将面板按正确顺序重新放入同样大小的网格中，保留 grey 分隔线。面板内容不做任何修改，仅改变其在网格中的位置。\\\\\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要将每个面板的四条边缘花纹视为\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"拼图接口\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"，通过逐对匹配边缘花纹来推断正确的空间排列。关键在于识别出边缘花纹是匹配线索，而非面板内部图案——内部图案是干扰项，真正决定排列的是边缘处的颜色序列。\\\\\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n- `description`：识别网格中每个\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"对象发射的十字射线，根据射线交叉点处的叠加规则确定交叉像素的最终颜色，再将每座塔按其实际覆盖的独占射线长度从长到短排序，输出为对应颜色的竖条。\\\\\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"，每座塔是一个 3*3 的单色实心方块，颜色各不相同。从每座塔的中心像素出发，向上、下、左、右四个方向发射与塔同色的射线，射线延伸至网格边界。当两条不同颜色的射线在某个像素交叉时，该像素显示为较大面积塔（3*3 方块面积不算，只看射线覆盖的总像素数更多的那座塔）的颜色。\\\\\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步：为每座塔画出从中心向四个方向延伸到网格边界的十字射线（不覆盖其他塔的 3*3 方块区域，射线遇到其他塔的方块时截断）。第二步：在射线交叉点处，比较两座塔各自的射线总长度（四个方向之和），用射线总长度较长的塔的颜色覆盖交叉像素。第三步：统计每座塔最终独占的射线像素数（被覆盖的不算），按独占数从大到小排序。第四步：输出一个 1*K 的网格（K 为塔的数量），每个像素按排序顺序填入对应塔的颜色。\\\\\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题需要三层推理——先构建射线并理解交叉处的覆盖规则（射线总长决定优先级），再统计覆盖后的独占像素数，最后将排序结果编码为颜色条。表面上看到的是彩色十字交叉图案，但规则的核心是\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"射线长度决定交叉优先级\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"这一非显然的叠加逻辑。\\\\\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\\\\\n- `description`：在由彩色路径连接的节点图中，每个节点根据与其相连的路径颜色混合规则变换自身颜色，路径本身则继承其两端节点变换后颜色的选择结果。\\\\\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个 2*2 的单色实心方块作为\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"节点\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"，节点颜色各不相同。节点之间通过单像素宽的彩色直线路径（水平或垂直）连接，每条路径有自己的颜色，且路径颜色与其两端节点的颜色都不同。n        return None\\\\\\\\n    return grid\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_111948_seed807260302/seed807260302__1__codegen_prompts__8.log:47:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/1/4.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport random\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\\\\\nGREY = 5\\\\\\\\nSEED_COLORS = (1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7)\\\\\\\\nMIN_ROOM_SIDE = 2\\\\\\\\nMAX_ROOM_SIDE = 6\\\\\\\\nMIN_ROOM_COUNT = 2\\\\\\\\nMAX_ROOM_COUNT = 4\\\\\\\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _interior_slices(length: int, line_indices: list[int]) -> list[slice]:\\\\\\\\n    boundaries = [-1] + sorted(int(i) for i in line_indices) + [int(length)]\\\\\\\\n    slices: list[slice] = []\\\\\\\\n    for a, b in zip(boundaries, boundaries[1:]):\\\\\\\\n        start = int(a + 1)\\\\\\\\n        stop = int(b)\\\\\\\\n        if start < stop:\\\\\\\\n            slices.append(slice(start, stop))\\\\\\\\n    return slices\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    Fill each grey-bounded room with the seed-anchored pattern selected by that room's aspect ratio.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\\\\\n    - Black background is cut by complete grey horizontal and vertical grid lines into rectangular rooms.\\\\\\\\n    - Each room interior contains exactly one colored seed pixel, and no other non-black cells.\\\\\\\\n    - The seed colors are non-black and non-grey; grey separator lines remain outside the room interiors.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Rule:\\\\\\\\n    - Measure each room's interior width W and height H, excluding grey separator lines.\\\\\\\\n    - If W > H, fill every other full row of the room with the seed color, anchored on the seed row.\\\\\\\\n    - If H > W, fill every other full column of the room with the seed color, anchored on the seed column.\\\\\\\\n    - If H = W, fill the seed-colored parity class of the checkerboard pattern anchored at the seed cell.\\\\\\\\n    - All unfilled room cells are black and all grey separator lines are preserved.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\\\\\n    - The room aspect ratio chooses horizontal stripes, vertical stripes, or checkerboard, while the seed position fixes the phase of that pattern.\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n    assert g.ndim == 2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"expected a 2D grid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    height, width = map(int, g.shape)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    grey_rows = [r for r in range(height) if bool(np.all(g[r, :] == GREY))]\\\\\\\\n    grey_cols = [c for c in range(width) if bool(np.all(g[:, c] == GREY))]\\\\\\\\n    row_slices = _interior_slices(height, grey_rows)\\\\\\\\n    col_slices = _interior_slices(width, grey_cols)\\\\\\\\n    assert row_slices and col_slices, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"expected at least one rectangular room\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\\\\\n    for rs in row_slices:\\\\\\\\n        for cs in col_slices:\\\\\\\\n            room = g[rs, cs]\\\\\\\\n            assert not np.any(room == GREY), \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"grey pixels must be separator lines only\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n            seed_mask = (room != BLACK) & (room != GREY)\\\\\\\\n            seeds = np.argwhere(seed_mask)\\\\\\\\n            assert len(seeds) == 1, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"each room must contain exactly one colored seed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n            local_r, local_c = map(int, seeds[0])\\\\\\\\n            seed_r = int(rs.start + local_r)\\\\\\\\n            seed_c = int(cs.start + local_c)\\\\\\\\n            color = int(room[local_r, local_c])\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n            room_h = int(rs.stop - rs.start)\\\\\\\\n            room_w = int(cs.stop - cs.start)\\\\\\\\n            out[rs, cs] = BLACK\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n            if room_w > room_h:\\\\\\\\n                for r in range(rs.start, rs.stop):\\\\\\\\n                    if (r - seed_r) % 2 == 0:\\\\\\\\n                        out[r, cs] = color\\\\\\\\n            elif room_h > room_w:\\\\\\\\n                for c in range(cs.start, cs.stop):\\\\\\\\n                    if (c - seed_c) % 2 == 0:\\\\\\\\n                        out[rs, c] = color\\\\\\\\n            else:\\\\\\\\n                rr, cc = np.indices((room_h, room_w))\\\\\\\\n                parity = (rr + cc - local_r - local_c) % 2 == 0\\\\\\\\n                patch = np.full((room_h, room_w), BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n                patch[parity] = color\\\\\\\\n                out[rs, cs] = patch\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    return out\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _room_sizes(count: int, required_a: int, required_b: int) -> list[int]:\\\\\\\\n    sizes = [int(required_a), int(required_b)]\\\\\\\\n    while len(sizes) < count:\\\\\\\\n        sizes.append(random.randint(MIN_ROOM_SIDE, MAX_ROOM_SIDE))\\\\\\\\n    random.shuffle(sizes)\\\\\\\\n    return sizes\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _boundaries(sizes: list[int]) -> list[int]:\\\\\\\\n    pos = 0\\\\\\\\n    result = [0]\\\\\\\\n    for size in sizes:\\\\\\\\n        pos += int(size) + 1\\\\\\\\n        result.append(pos)\\\\\\\\n    return result\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _paint_grid_lines(grid: np.ndarray, row_bounds: list[int], col_bounds: list[int]) -> None:\\\\\\\\n    for r in row_bounds:\\\\\\\\n        grid[int(r), :] = GREY\\\\\\\\n    for c in col_bounds:\\\\\\\\n        grid[:, int(c)] = GREY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _room_intervals(bounds: list[int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\\\\\\\n    return [(int(a + 1), int(b)) for a, b in zip(bounds, bounds[1:]) if int(a + 1) < int(b)]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _has_all_branches(row_sizes: list[int], col_sizes: list[int]) -> bool:\\\\\\\\n    branches = set()\\\\\\\\n    for h in row_sizes:\\\\\\\\n        for w in col_sizes:\\\\\\\\n            if w > h:\\\\\\\\n                branches.add(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wide\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n            elif h > w:\\\\\\\\n                branches.add(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tall\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n            else:\\\\\\\\n                branches.add(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"square\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n    return branches == {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wide\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tall\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"square\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\\\\\n    row_count = random.randint(MIN_ROOM_COUNT, MAX_ROOM_COUNT)\\\\\\\\n    col_count = random.randint(MIN_ROOM_COUNT, MAX_ROOM_COUNT)\\\\\\\\n    a, b = random.sample(range(MIN_ROOM_SIDE, MAX_ROOM_SIDE + 1), 2)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    row_sizes = _room_sizes(row_count, a, b)\\\\\\\\n    col_sizes = _room_sizes(col_count, a, b)\\\\\\\\n    if not _has_all_branches(row_sizes, col_sizes):\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    row_bounds = _boundaries(row_sizes)\\\\\\\\n    col_bounds = _boundaries(col_sizes)\\\\\\\\n    height = int(row_bounds[-1] + 1)\\\\\\\\n    width = int(col_bounds[-1] + 1)\\\\\\\\n    if max(height, width) > 30:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    grid = np.full((height, width), BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n    _paint_grid_lines(grid, row_bounds, col_bounds)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    row_intervals = _room_intervals(row_bounds)\\\\\\\\n    col_intervals = _room_intervals(col_bounds)\\\\\\\\n    for r0, r1 in row_intervals:\\\\\\\\n        for c0, c1 in col_intervals:\\\\\\\\n            sr = random.randint(r0, r1 - 1)\\\\\\\\n            sc = random.randint(c0, c1 - 1)\\\\\\\\n            grid[sr, sc] = random.choice(SEED_COLORS)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    try:\\\\\\\\n        out = main(grid)\\\\\\\\n    except AssertionError:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n    if not isinstance(out, np.ndarray) or out.shape != grid.shape or max(out.shape) > 30:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n    return grid\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\\\\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\\\\\\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\\\\\\\n        if grid is not None:\\\\\\\\n            return grid\\\\\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed to generate a valid seed807260302/1/4 input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/13/codegen_prompts/1.md:279:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/13/codegen_prompts/1.md:287:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/runaste(grid, legend, r0, c0)\\\\\\\\n    return grid\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _build_sprite_queue(\\\\\\\\n    key_colors: list[int],\\\\\\\\n    counts: list[int],\\\\\\\\n    distractor_color: int | None,\\\\\\\\n    bg: int,\\\\\\\\n) -> list[np.ndarray]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Create canonical key sprites, optional distractor sprite, and shuffle them.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    sprites = []\\\\\\\\n    for color, count in zip(key_colors, counts):\\\\\\\\n        sprite = _make_sprite(color, bg)\\\\\\\\n        for _ in range(count):\\\\\\\\n            sprites.append(sprite.copy())\\\\\\\\n    if distractor_color is not None:\\\\\\\\n        sprites.append(_make_sprite(distractor_color, bg))\\\\\\\\n    random.shuffle(sprites)\\\\\\\\n    return sprites\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _place_sprites(grid: np.ndarray, sprites: list[np.ndarray], bg: int) -> None:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Paste sprites into random non-touching free locations in queue order.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    for sprite in sprites:\\\\\\\\n        sr, sc = random_free_location(\\\\\\\\n            grid,\\\\\\\\n            sprite,\\\\\\\\n            transparent=bg,\\\\\\\\n            padding=SPRITE_PADDING,\\\\\\\\n            padding_connectivity=SPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY,\\\\\\\\n        )\\\\\\\\n        paste(grid, sprite, sr, sc, transparent=bg)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Run one output-first generation attempt and reject solver mismatches.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    bg, key_colors, distractor_color = _sample_palette()\\\\\\\\n    counts = _sample_counts(len(key_colors))\\\\\\\\n    expected = _build_expected(key_colors, counts)\\\\\\\\n    legend = _build_legend(expected.shape, key_colors)\\\\\\\\n    grid = _new_grid_with_legend(bg, legend)\\\\\\\\n    if grid is None:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    sprites = _build_sprite_queue(key_colors, counts, distractor_color, bg)\\\\\\\\n    try:\\\\\\\\n        _place_sprites(grid, sprites, bg)\\\\\\\\n    except ValueError:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    if not np.array_equal(main(grid), expected):\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001243/5_5.log:1872:3. 在辅助框内部，把“被修正像素在其所属半区内的局部坐标”标成红色，这样左右/上下两侧的瑕疵都能统一投影到同尺寸辅助区。\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_111948_seed807260302/seed807260302__5__codegen_prompts__7.log:7:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/45a5af55.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    Build nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\\\\\n    - Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\\\\\\\n    - Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Rule:\\\\\\\\n    - Read stripes bottom to top.\\\\\\\\n    - Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\\\\\\\\n    - Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    Key insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n    H, _W = g.shape\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Parse stripe runs from bottom to top.\\\\\\\\n    runs: list[tuple[int, int]] = []  # (color, height), bottom -> top\\\\\\\\n    r = int(H - 1)\\\\\\\\n    while r >= 0:\\\\\\\\n        col = int(g[int(r), 0])\\\\\\\\n        h = 1\\\\\\\\n        rr = int(r - 1)\\\\\\\\n        while rr >= 0 and bool((g[int(rr)] == int(col)).all()):\\\\\\\\n            h += 1\\\\\\\\n            rr -= 1\\\\\\\\n        runs.append((int(col), int(h)))\\\\\\\\n        r = int(rr)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    assert not (not runs)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    c0, h0 = runs[0]\\\\\\\\n    cur = np.full((int(h0), int(h0)), int(c0), dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    for col, h in runs[1:]:\\\\\\\\n        h = int(h)\\\\\\\\n        new_n = int(cur.shape[0] + 2 * h)\\\\\\\\n        nxt = np.full((new_n, new_n), int(col), dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n        nxt[h : h + cur.shape[0], h : h + cur.shape[1]] = cur\\\\\\\\n        cur = nxt\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    return cur\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\\\\\n    W = int(np.random.randint(6, 15))\\\\\\\\n    n_runs = int(np.random.randint(2, 7))\\\\\\\\n    heights = [int(np.random.randint(1, 5)) for _ in range(n_runs)]\\\\\\\\n    if heights[0] + 2 * sum(heights[1:]) > 30:\\\\\\\\n        return None\\\\\\\\n    cols: list[int] = []\\\\\\\\n    prev = None\\\\\\\\n    for _ in range(n_runs):\\\\\\\\n        c = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\\\\\\\n        while prev is not None and c == prev:\\\\\\\\n            c = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\\\\\\\n        cols.append(c)\\\\\\\\n        prev = c\\\\\\\\n    stripes = [np.full((h, W), col, dtype=int) for col, h in reversed(list(zip(cols, heights)))]\\\\\\\\n    return np.vstack(stripes)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef generate_in